{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TracelessDifferenceEllipticity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TracelessDifferenceEllipticity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.threshold_pos_of_both_hyperbolic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.threshold_pos_of_both_hyperbolic","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TracelessDifferenceEllipticity.lean#L89-L95","doc":"Two hyperbolic directions force a strictly positive alignment threshold, so\nthe difference cannot be elliptic \"for free\" — the pairing has to be large. This\nis what makes the measured `2.107175 > 2.098162` a statement about the nucleons\nrather than a generic fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.sub_elliptic_iff_pairing_large","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.sub_elliptic_iff_pairing_large","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TracelessDifferenceEllipticity.lean#L79-L87","doc":"The ellipticity criterion in Killing-pairing form: the difference of two\ntraceless directions is elliptic (`det > 0`) exactly when their pairing exceeds\nminus the sum of their determinants. For two **hyperbolic** directions\n(`det A₀, det B₀ < 0`) that threshold is positive, so alignment is required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.det_sub_traceless","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.det_sub_traceless","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TracelessDifferenceEllipticity.lean#L70-L77","doc":"**The mechanism.** For traceless `2 × 2` matrices written out by entries,\n`det (A₀ − B₀) = det A₀ + det B₀ + tr (A₀ B₀)`, where a traceless\n`(x, y; z, −x)` has `det = −x² − yz` and\n`tr (A₀ B₀) = 2ad + bf + ce`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}